# Guardrail attach point #2 of 2 — GATEWAY-ENFORCED via promptGuard.
#
# Here the GATEWAY calls Bedrock's ApplyGuardrail API out-of-band: on the request before it
# reaches the model, and on the response before it reaches the client. The model call itself
# carries no guardrail (this policy targets the route whose backend is the UNguarded
# bedrock-llama3-8b), so anything blocked here was blocked by the gateway.
#
# Three consequences worth knowing, all of them differences from the native form in 12-:
#
#  1. `region` is REQUIRED here. The native form inherits the provider's region; this filter has
#     no provider to inherit from, so the region is explicit. Point it at a region where the
#     guardrail does not exist and you get a failure that looks like an auth problem.
#  2. It authenticates SEPARATELY. `policies.auth.aws` below is this filter's own credential —
#     not the backend's. Omit it and the guardrail call falls back to whatever ambient AWS
#     credentials the proxy has, which is usually none, while the model call keeps working on
#     the backend's secret. That asymmetry is the interesting failure mode to probe: one
#     credential for the model, another for the guard.
#  3. A block is the GATEWAY's response, so the status code is ours to choose (below) rather
#     than Bedrock's intervention body. That is what makes these tests assertable on a code.
#
# Each promptGuard list item holds EXACTLY ONE filter type (CRD rule:
# ExactlyOneOf=regex;webhook;openAIModeration;bedrockGuardrails;googleModelArmor). `response` is
# not part of that set — it is the custom deny response for the filter in the same item, which is
# why it sits alongside rather than in its own entry. Several filter types = several items.
apiVersion: enterpriseagentgateway.solo.io/v1alpha1
kind: EnterpriseAgentgatewayPolicy
metadata:
  name: bedrock-promptguard
  namespace: agentgateway-system
spec:
  targetRefs:
    - group: gateway.networking.k8s.io
      kind: HTTPRoute
      name: bedrock-guard-promptguard
  backend:
    ai:
      promptGuard:
        request:
          - bedrockGuardrails:
              identifier: %%BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_ID%%
              version: "%%BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_VERSION%%"
              region: us-west-2                  # REQUIRED here — nothing to inherit from
              policies:
                auth:
                  aws:
                    secretRef:
                      name: bedrock-secret       # this filter's OWN credential (see note 2)
            response:
              message: "blocked by bedrock guardrail on the request"
              statusCode: 403
        response:
          - bedrockGuardrails:
              identifier: %%BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_ID%%
              version: "%%BEDROCK_GUARDRAIL_VERSION%%"
              region: us-west-2
              policies:
                auth:
                  aws:
                    secretRef:
                      name: bedrock-secret
            response:
              message: "blocked by bedrock guardrail on the response"
              statusCode: 403
